            'title' => 'Experience is a starting point, not an answer',
            'image_alt' => 'A figure in a dark coat, seen from behind, stands in the doorway of a violet study with a lamp and bookshelves, holding a blank pane of glass toward a teal night lake.',
            'excerpt' => 'The second volume of Sunday metaphysics, dated 4 October 2026, does not crown a winning doctrine. It shows where experience, scientific description and a claim about the nature of the world get confused: in consciousness, the person, time, freedom and spiritual knowledge.',
